# Pull request (as of the branch head in this repo)

Branch: fix/same-currency-requests into main.

## Title
Round payment requests in the tab's own currency

## Description
A member who pays in the tab's own currency was asked for the exact balance. An uneven split leaves a fraction of a cent on it: when three members split 10.00, each of the other two has a balance of 3.3333, and the bank rejects a payment request for 3.3333 EUR. Requests in another currency were not affected, because `request_amount` already rounds them after the conversion.

Change: the same-currency branch of `request_amount` now also goes through `to_minor`, as the converted branch already does.

Validation: `test_same_currency_request_is_rounded` fails on main (`Decimal('3.333333333333333333333333333')` instead of `Decimal('3.33')`) and passes with the fix. The other tests are unchanged.


## Inline review thread on tabsplit/settle.py

Anchored to line 14 as of @FIX_SHA@:

    +        # Same currency, but the amount is still rounded.

### dkemper at 2026-11-17T09:12:44Z

